WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.480
Hello, my name is Angus Willows, and I want to tell you a little bit about my experience

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:19.280
with the Amazon FBA, and give you a few golden nuggets of information that I've learned along

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:19.915
the way.

00:00:19.915 --> 00:00:24.360
In college, I invented the kangaroo hanger, which is essentially a big paper clip

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.258
that clips in all of your clothes.

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:29.240
The kangaroo hanger was first produced in Asia, and I started

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.769
out selling it on Amazon about two years ago, using Amazon FBA.

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:34.240
Then, about a year and

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.920
a half ago, we transitioned to US manufacturing, and we're still using FBA because it just

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.216
makes the most sense financially for the business.

00:00:42.216 --> 00:00:44.800
One of the main benefits of Amazon FBA, which

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.000
I'm sure you've heard of before, is the prime badge.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.600
When I'm shopping online and

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.640
there's something that I need urgently, and it says it's going to be delivered in a week

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.573
or two weeks, I usually just skip over that and move on to something else.

00:00:59.573 --> 00:01:00.560
And so that's

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.960
why it's so critical to have the prime badge on Amazon, and one of the best ways to get

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.440
that is through FBA.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.880
The kangaroo hanger is made and shipped from Wisconsin, and so the

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:18.040
benefit of that is we can fulfill individual customer orders from our Wisconsin facility.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:23.720
But we've actually found that using Amazon FBA is cheaper, so shipping the product to

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.800
Amazon, and then having them fulfill it to the end customer is actually cheaper for us

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.512
than shipping it directly to the end customer from our facility in Wisconsin.

00:01:33.512 --> 00:01:34.600
And one of

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:40.080
the main reasons for that is because Amazon gets significant discounts on their shipping.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:48.120
So the cost of shipping on Amazon is significantly lower than even wholesale rates from carriers

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:48.770
like UPS.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:51.695
Here's my main tip when starting out with FBA.

00:01:51.695 --> 00:01:53.320
You don't necessarily need to

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.360
go all in.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.560
What we did with kangaroo hanger was we started out by shipping only our top

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:05.016
selling SKUs to Amazon FBA and having them fulfilled through Amazon.

00:02:05.016 --> 00:02:07.000
And we kept our

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.600
slower selling SKUs as in-house Amazon fulfilled by merchant.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.360
Thanks for watching, and if you

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.640
ever need hangers, keep an eye out for the kangaroo hanger.
